            booksFaqTitle:"Frequently asked questions", booksFaq1Question:"What is the best self-help book to read?", booksFaq1Answer:"Atomic Habits by James Clear is the most actionable modern self-help book. For timeless philosophy, Meditations by Marcus Aurelius remains the gold standard.", booksFaq2Question:"Are these books worth reading in 2026?", booksFaq2Answer:"Yes. Each book has been re-read and recommended because the ideas compound over time, not because they are trendy.", booksFaq3Question:"Do you earn a commission from these links?", booksFaq3Answer:"Yes. As an Amazon Associate, we earn from qualifying purchases. The price you pay is unchanged.",
            focusBooksKicker:"The Bookstand · Best Of", focusBooksTitle:"Best Books on <em>Focus & Deep Work</em>", focusBooksSubtitle:"The books that teach attention as a craft — how to do hard things, on purpose, for a long time.",
            focusAffiliateHeading:"Affiliate Disclosure:", focusAffiliateText:"As an Amazon Associate, we earn from qualifying purchases made through the Amazon links on this page. The price you pay is unchanged. We only recommend books we've personally read and found genuinely valuable — never paid placements.", focusAffiliateLink:"Read our full disclosure policy →",
            focusWhyFail:"Why focus books fail", focusWhyFailP1:"Most productivity books sell motivation. These sell attention. The difference matters: motivation is a feeling, attention is a trainable skill. Deep Work defines the skill, The Practicing Mind defines the training, and Focused Work defines the daily architecture.", focusWhyFailP2:"If you want a practical protocol before buying the books, read our", focusDeepWorkLink:"Deep Work protocol", focus90DayLink:"90-day identity test", focusTwoMinLink:"2-Minute Rule guide", focusBrowseFull:"Browse the full collection:", focusBestBooksLink:"best self-help books", focusBestHabitLink:"best habit books", focusBestStoicismLink:"best stoicism books",
